      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Aflatoxins are hepatotoxic mycotoxins (mold toxins) and are the most commonly reported cause of mycotoxicosis associated with pet food. The four major forms of aflatoxin in feedstuffs are aflatoxin B1, B2, G1, and G2. Aflatoxin B1 is the most common and most toxic.",
              "pdf_page": 1008,
              "printed_page": 926,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
